       "encoded‐pub‐key" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__EENNCCOODDEEDD__PPUUBBLLIICC__KKEEYY) <octet string>
           Used for getting and setting the encoding of the DH public key used
           in  a  key  exchange   message   for   the   TLS   protocol.    See
           EEVVPP__PPKKEEYY__sseett11__eennccooddeedd__ppuubblliicc__kkeeyy(())                              and
           EEVVPP__PPKKEEYY__ggeett11__eennccooddeedd__ppuubblliicc__kkeeyy(()).

   DDHH aaddddiittiioonnaall ddoommaaiinn ppaarraammeetteerrss
       "safeprime‐generator" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__DDHH__GGEENNEERRAATTOORR) <integer>
           Used for DH generation of safe primes  using  the  old  safe  prime
           generator  code.  The default value is 2.  It is recommended to use
           a named safe prime group instead, if domain parameter validation is
           required.

           Randomly generated safe primes are not allowed by FIPS, so  setting
           this  value  for  the  OpenSSL  FIPS provider will instead choose a
           named safe prime group based on the size of _p.

   DDHH aanndd DDHHXX ddoommaaiinn ppaarraammeetteerr // kkeeyy ggeenneerraattiioonn ppaarraammeetteerrss
       In addition to the common FFC key generation parameters  that  all  FFC
       key  types  should  support  (see  "FFC  key  generation parameters" in
       EEVVPP__PPKKEEYY--FFFFCC(7)) the DDHH and DDHHXX  keytype  implementation  supports  the
       following:

       "type" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__FFFFCC__TTYYPPEE) <UTF8 string>
           Sets the type of parameter generation. For DDHH valid values are:

           "fips186_4"
           "default"
           "fips186_2"
               These  are  described  in  "FFC  key  generation parameters" in
               EEVVPP__PPKKEEYY--FFFFCC(7)

           "group"
               This specifies that a named safe  prime  name  will  be  chosen
               using the "pbits" type.

           "generator"
               A  safe  prime  generator.  See  the "safeprime‐generator" type
               above.  This is only valid for DDHH keys.

       "pbits" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__FFFFCC__PPBBIITTSS) <unsigned integer>
           Sets the size (in bits) of the prime ’p’.

           For "fips186_4" this must be 2048.  For "fips186_2"  this  must  be
           1024.  For "group" this can be any one of 2048, 3072, 4096, 6144 or
           8192.

       "priv_len" (OOSSSSLL__PPKKEEYY__PPAARRAAMM__DDHH__PPRRIIVV__LLEENN) <integer>
           An  optional  value  to  set  the  maximum  length of the generated
           private key.  The default value used if this  is  not  set  is  the
           maximum  value  of BN_num_bits(_q)). The minimum value that this can
           be set to is 2 * s.  Where s is the security strength  of  the  key
           which  has  values  of  112, 128, 152, 176 and 200 for key sizes of
           2048, 3072, 4096, 6144 and 8192.

